[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 SDD (Software Design Description) - ADAS Control Module
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
 Scope
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
1 Identification
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-001
TITLE: Design Document Identification
STATEMENT: This document shall be identified as the Software Design Description (SDD) for the Advanced Driver Assistance System (ADAS) Control Module, version 1.0, following MIL-STD-498 and ISO 26262 standards.
RATIONALE: Proper document identification ensures configuration management and design traceability for safety-critical automotive systems.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
2 System overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-002
TITLE: Design Overview
STATEMENT: The ADAS Control Module software design shall implement a safety-critical, real-time architecture with redundant processing paths, sensor fusion algorithms, and fault-tolerant communication for automotive driver assistance applications.
RATIONALE: Architectural overview establishes the foundation for detailed design specifications in the automotive safety domain.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
3 Document overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-003
TITLE: Design Document Structure
STATEMENT: This document shall be organized into sections covering design overview, architectural design, detailed design, interface design, and design constraints following MIL-STD-498 and automotive safety standards.
RATIONALE: Structured organization facilitates design review and implementation guidance for safety-critical systems.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 2
 Referenced documents
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-004
TITLE: Design References
STATEMENT: The design shall reference the SRS document, ISO 26262 safety standards, AUTOSAR architecture standards, MISRA C++ guidelines, and automotive cybersecurity standards for design implementation.
RATIONALE: Design references ensure consistency with requirements and established automotive safety patterns.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
 CSCI-wide design decisions
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-005
TITLE: Safety Architecture Decision
STATEMENT: The system shall implement a dual-redundant architecture with independent processing paths, sensor fusion algorithms, and voting mechanisms to ensure safety and reliability.
RATIONALE: Dual-redundant architecture provides fault tolerance and meets ASIL D safety requirements.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-006
TITLE: Real-Time Architecture Decision
STATEMENT: The system shall use a real-time operating system with deterministic scheduling, priority-based task management, and bounded response times for safety-critical functions.
RATIONALE: Real-time architecture ensures predictable system behavior and meets automotive timing requirements.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-007
TITLE: Technology Stack Decision
STATEMENT: The system shall use MISRA C++ compliant code, AUTOSAR middleware, secure communication protocols, and automotive-grade development tools for implementation.
RATIONALE: Selected technology stack ensures safety compliance, performance, and operational reliability.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
 CSCI architectural design
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
1 CSCI components
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-008
TITLE: Sensor Fusion Component
STATEMENT: The Sensor Fusion Component shall integrate data from multiple sensors (radar, camera, ultrasonic) using Kalman filtering, object tracking algorithms, and confidence scoring for environmental perception.
RATIONALE: Dedicated sensor fusion component ensures accurate environmental perception and safety system operation.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-009
TITLE: Decision Making Component
STATEMENT: The Decision Making Component shall implement safety-critical decision algorithms for lane departure, collision avoidance, and adaptive cruise control with redundant processing paths.
RATIONALE: Centralized decision making component ensures consistent safety-critical behavior across all ADAS functions.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-010
TITLE: Vehicle Control Component
STATEMENT: The Vehicle Control Component shall provide secure interfaces to vehicle systems (brakes, steering, engine) with safety interlocks and command validation.
RATIONALE: Vehicle control component enables ADAS functions to influence vehicle behavior safely and securely.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-011
TITLE: Human Machine Interface Component
STATEMENT: The Human Machine Interface Component shall provide driver warnings, system status, and configuration options through multiple display interfaces with priority-based messaging.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive HMI component enables efficient system operation and driver awareness.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-012
TITLE: Safety Monitor Component
STATEMENT: The Safety Monitor Component shall continuously monitor system health, detect faults, and implement graceful degradation with automatic failover to safe states.
RATIONALE: Safety monitor component ensures system reliability and compliance with automotive safety standards.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
2 Concept of execution
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-013
TITLE: Real-Time Execution Model
STATEMENT: The system shall execute as a multi-threaded real-time application with priority-based scheduling, deterministic timing, and bounded response times for safety-critical tasks.
RATIONALE: Real-time execution model ensures predictable system behavior and meets automotive timing requirements.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-014
TITLE: Safety Execution Model
STATEMENT: The system shall implement watchdog timers, health monitoring, and automatic recovery mechanisms with graceful degradation to safe operating modes.
RATIONALE: Safety execution model ensures system reliability and compliance with automotive safety standards.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
3 Interface design
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4.3
1 Interface identification and diagrams
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-015
TITLE: Sensor Interface Design
STATEMENT: The system shall provide standardized sensor interfaces supporting CAN bus, Ethernet, and FlexRay protocols with data validation, error detection, and redundancy management.
RATIONALE: Standardized sensor interfaces enable system integration and ensure data reliability.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-016
TITLE: Vehicle Control Interface Design
STATEMENT: The system shall provide secure vehicle control interfaces with command validation, safety interlocks, and redundant communication paths for critical vehicle functions.
RATIONALE: Secure vehicle control interfaces ensure safe operation and prevent unauthorized vehicle control.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-017
TITLE: HMI Interface Design
STATEMENT: The system shall provide configurable HMI interfaces supporting multiple display types with priority-based messaging, driver distraction management, and accessibility features.
RATIONALE: Configurable HMI interfaces ensure driver awareness and system transparency.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 5
 Software unit detailed design
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-018
TITLE: Lane Detection Module
STATEMENT: The Lane Detection Module shall implement computer vision algorithms for lane boundary detection, lane departure prediction, and lane keeping assistance with sub-pixel accuracy.
RATIONALE: Advanced lane detection algorithms ensure accurate lane departure warning and correction.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-019
TITLE: Object Detection Module
STATEMENT: The Object Detection Module shall implement deep learning algorithms for vehicle, pedestrian, and obstacle detection with real-time processing and confidence scoring.
RATIONALE: Advanced object detection algorithms ensure accurate collision warning and avoidance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-020
TITLE: Trajectory Planning Module
STATEMENT: The Trajectory Planning Module shall implement path planning algorithms for adaptive cruise control and emergency maneuvers with safety constraints and smooth trajectories.
RATIONALE: Advanced trajectory planning ensures smooth and safe vehicle control.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-021
TITLE: Traffic Sign Recognition Module
STATEMENT: The Traffic Sign Recognition Module shall implement image processing algorithms for traffic sign detection and classification with high accuracy and real-time performance.
RATIONALE: Advanced traffic sign recognition enhances driver awareness and compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-022
TITLE: Safety Monitor Module
STATEMENT: The Safety Monitor Module shall implement comprehensive system health monitoring, fault detection, and automatic recovery mechanisms with configurable thresholds.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive safety monitoring ensures system reliability and compliance with automotive standards.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 6
 Requirements traceability
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-023
TITLE: Design Traceability
STATEMENT: All design elements shall be traceable to software requirements through a comprehensive traceability matrix linking components, modules, and requirements with safety impact analysis.
RATIONALE: Requirements traceability ensures complete requirement coverage and facilitates change impact analysis for safety-critical systems.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 7
 Notes
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-024
TITLE: Implementation Guidelines
STATEMENT: The software shall be implemented using MISRA C++ compliant code with static analysis, code reviews, unit testing, and continuous integration practices for quality assurance.
RATIONALE: Implementation guidelines provide guidance for development teams and ensure code quality and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
